    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup for May 17 centers on the favorable matchup against Young, where **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leads the charge with an elite 73.66 rating. His massive 14% platoon boost, paired with an advantageous order slot, makes him the premier start of the day. **Josh Lowe** (71.68) also provides high-ceiling production despite hitting seventh; the combination of a weak opposing starter in Sasaki and a significant 14% platoon edge elevates his value well above his base projection. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (67.71) and **Drake Baldwin** (66.59) remain high-floor staples, with the latter benefiting from a leadoff position and a friendly matchup against Bello.\n\nStrategic decisions were particularly tight in the utility and outfield slots. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** earns a strong 63.93 score, maintaining his position despite a minor platoon drag, while **Jackson Merrill** remains a potential risk factor; his 56.95 score relies on an assumed leadoff role, but the matchup against Kirby is treacherous given the pitcher's elite skill set and the unfavorable park factors. The most difficult exclusion from the starting nine was **Dominic Smith** (56.83). While he maintains a solid profile against Bello, he was ultimately edged out by the superior plate appearance quality projected for our active starters. **Sam Antonacci** warrants monitoring as he faces Rea; while he offers an elite 0.400 xwOBA, the wind blowing in could dampen his efficiency, despite his strong 7% platoon advantage.",
